            <div xml:id="d337">

                <pb facs="0426" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/562: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Maginnis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-10T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 10,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Your March 4, 10 p.m.</p>
                <p>You are authorized to state that no such statement as you refer to was made by
                    the Under Secretary or any other official of this Department.</p>
                <p>You will seek an early opportunity to intimate to the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs that in the opinion of the Department, Bolivia is injuring her own
                    interests as regards access to the sea by taking up that question before any
                    definite step has been taken toward the settlement of the pending controversy
                    between Peru and Chile.</p>
                <p>Your February 10, 6 p.m.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d337-f1"/></p>
                <p>Have you unmistakable evidence of deportation of Peruvians and is such
                    deportation continuing and in what numbers? If such deportation continues you
                    may at your discretion, call attention of the Minister for Foreign Affairs to
                    the bitter feeling which this policy will arouse.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
